Settle custody per unit, retry refused submits, and carry every shell family

Admission is local queue ownership; each unit now gets a ticket whose
custody (Queued, InFlight, Submitted, Stored, Written, Refused, Unknown,
DroppedUnsent) the connection reports, through additive *_tracked methods
beside the existing Result<()> ones. A file-wire record is Submitted only
when its Submitted event is observed, which may precede the submit reply;
a unit stays queued until settled, and a disconnect classifies it. A submit
refused with EAGAIN keeps its staged record and goes again after a consumed
event or a doubling backoff, never in the same pass; EALREADY is custody
only after an observed Submitted; ESTALE is revocation; any other error is
a definitive refusal and the lane moves on. Slot writes back off the same
way and settle as Stored.

Snapshot objects: each announcement holds acknowledgement at the earliest
unfetched announcement per feed; an announcement already superseded in the
buffered events is not fetched; an opened object whose qid differs is
newer and delivers nothing; reads continue to a zero-length end, respecting
iounit, with a 1-byte probe at the feed's cap; the decoded generation must
match; node ESTALE or EAGAIN restarts a fetch twice at most. The catalog
and indicator objects and their activation outcomes, indicator and catalog
activations, action responses and catalog candidates now ride the file
wire.
